                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "18302bc3-c103-312b-b60d-500e4fdd1533",
                        "entry_id": "8efd55d9-dc2c-376e-ad0b-51194a530a63",
                        "glosses": [
                            "witziger, treffender Ausspruch, Sinnspruch"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Rhetorik"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "bd405b64-230e-4eeb-8896-e6dbcb1a7ff3",
                                "sense_id": "18302bc3-c103-312b-b60d-500e4fdd1533",
                                "text": "„Nach einigen punktierten Zeilen, welche die Lücke bezeichnen, liest man: ›Nichts ist trauriger auf dieser Welt, als ein Dummkopf zu sein …‹ Wars Jakob, der dieses Apophthegma über seine Lippen brachte, oder war es sein Herr? Das könnte der Gegenstand einer langen und schwierigen Dissertation werden.“"
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ce5d9968-c7d8-45b8-b542-2d72626143f4",
                        "source_entry_id": "8efd55d9-dc2c-376e-ad0b-51194a530a63",
                        "source_sense_id": "18302bc3-c103-312b-b60d-500e4fdd1533",
                        "source_sense_description": "Rhetorik: witziger, treffender Ausspruch, Sinnspruch",
                        "target_lang_word": "apothegm",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "apothegm",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b5906e88-53dd-3353-b042-d05aed021315",
                                        "entry_id": "a7b3f5a6-c853-3886-86db-0cadc910b99d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A short, witty, instructive saying; an aphorism or maxim."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6c36c48a-bcde-4340-b291-329848671fd5",
                                                "sense_id": "b5906e88-53dd-3353-b042-d05aed021315",
                                                "text": "Every glaſs of wine, or bit almoſt, that I committed to my mouth, ſhe uſhered thither with ſome Apothegm or other: the whole ſeries, indeed, of her diſcourſe, was compoſed of nothing but reaſon or wit, which made me admire her; which ſhe eaſily underſtood, I perceived by her ſmiles, when ſhe obſerved me gaping, as it were, when ſhe ſpoke, as if I would have eaten up her Words."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "62d2e6f6-432f-406c-a5dd-0b3946317270",
                                                "sense_id": "b5906e88-53dd-3353-b042-d05aed021315",
                                                "text": "The account which he [James Ferguson] himself gives of these observations is exceedingly interesting, and strikingly brings out the ingenuity of his mind, and his determination to allow no difficulties of circumstances to stand in his way. [...] Thus we are reminded of the apothegm that where there's a will there's a way—an apothegm which has found illustration in every department of effort, but nowhere more frequently than in the progress of science and art."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a15ba2b0-21ba-4a2a-8ecd-df4e70a4a56b",
                                                "sense_id": "b5906e88-53dd-3353-b042-d05aed021315",
                                                "text": "\"You are too wonderful!\" he would say. \"How do you find time for everything?\"\nShe rejoined with the apophthegm that made the rounds of Riseholme next day.\n\"My dear, it is just busy people that have time for everything.\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "de7197ee-618f-4469-ab72-2350f6ae6485",
                                                "sense_id": "b5906e88-53dd-3353-b042-d05aed021315",
                                                "text": "For the gods have withheld from the barbarians the light of discretion, as that their poetry is not, like ours, full of choice apophthegms and useful maxims, but is all of love and war."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "afd52f3f-ba56-4604-be6f-5d14d48b2d67",
                                                "sense_id": "b5906e88-53dd-3353-b042-d05aed021315",
                                                "text": "The gnomic belief that the world is conditioned by love is no idle apothegm."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7fb08967-bb23-4c60-b8ec-1a009d03223a",
                                                "sense_id": "b5906e88-53dd-3353-b042-d05aed021315",
                                                "text": "Which means roughly that business keeps one safe from love—ominous talk when one’s lover is a courtesan. I hoped that it was just another literary conceit I ought to know. (It is, I later learned, an apothegm by Ovid.)"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "fe5d3c5c-c5c1-4622-86f6-1250a580fb35",
                        "source_entry_id": "8efd55d9-dc2c-376e-ad0b-51194a530a63",
                        "source_sense_id": "18302bc3-c103-312b-b60d-500e4fdd1533",
                        "source_sense_description": "Rhetorik: witziger, treffender Ausspruch, Sinnspruch",
                        "target_lang_word": "apophthegme",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "apophthegme",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a02cf651-2aa0-3f0c-8451-8b8a09cc25d4",
                                        "entry_id": "9ca9f874-2f7f-3598-b793-ad8834e70567",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Variante de apophtegme."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "dated"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "986bc54c-7ca1-4049-b53d-b8e81e549d48",
                                                "sense_id": "a02cf651-2aa0-3f0c-8451-8b8a09cc25d4",
                                                "text": "L’auteur s’interroge sur le parallélisme surprenant qui existe entre un passage de la troisième lettre de Pacôme et l’apophthegme d’Isidore IX, sachant qu’Isidore a vécu deux générations après Pacôme."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "373ba133-5f2c-41f8-af33-d828162cc9f6",
                                                "sense_id": "a02cf651-2aa0-3f0c-8451-8b8a09cc25d4",
                                                "text": "— Vous avez raison, dit madame Marneffe que cette crise effrayait et qui ne se souvenait plus d’avoir émis cet apophthegme."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "81ed3164-f6c6-4cb9-96c7-cfa0a2dca9c5",
                                                "sense_id": "a02cf651-2aa0-3f0c-8451-8b8a09cc25d4",
                                                "text": "Seulement le symbole rendait plus visible le sens caché, et Blazius, à qui la langue démangeait, se mit à moraliser sur ce thème avec force citations, apophthegmes et maximes que ses rôles de pédant lui suppéditaient en la mémoire."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0a0b3d79-4e05-4cbf-901b-bf9604436e35",
                                                "sense_id": "a02cf651-2aa0-3f0c-8451-8b8a09cc25d4",
                                                "text": "La vraie citation, la citation par excellence, […]. Elle n’est pas le fait du pédant qui, d’une main lourde et maladroite, jette un apophthegme ou un proverbe bien vulgaire, avec cet argument pour lui sans réplique : Magister dixit."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6cfba910-d113-409b-b95c-6b2b03d1b6e7",
                                                "sense_id": "a02cf651-2aa0-3f0c-8451-8b8a09cc25d4",
                                                "text": "Immédiatement après les cinq kings viennent les quatre livres moraux : […] ; un troisième se compose de discours et d'apophthegmes recueillis de la bouche de Confucius lui-même."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
